    <%# EJS DOCUMENTATION: https://ejs.co/ %>
    COMMENT: ====================================================================================
    COMMENT: CUSTOM METHODS FOR Execute OBJECT
    COMMENT: ====================================================================================
    
    COMMENT: Sets the component to be executed.
    METHOD setComponent(componentModel: BaseComponent)
        
        PURPOSE: Attaches a component model instance and formats it for server transmission
        
        PARAMETERS:
            componentModel: A component model instance with all required properties set
        
        WHY: Execute objects wrap components so they can be batched and sent together
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Store reference to the component
            SET this.componentModel TO componentModel
            
            COMMENT: Extract and store the component name
            SET this.component TO componentModel.objectName
            
            COMMENT: Store parameters using the best available serialization method
            IF componentModel has method prepareForJson THEN
                SET this.parameters TO componentModel.prepareForJson()
            ELSE IF componentModel has method toObject THEN
                SET this.parameters TO componentModel.toObject()
            ELSE
                SET this.parameters TO null
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: Note: parameters is always this component's plain, unencrypted form.
            COMMENT: Whether the request ends up sending {component, parameters} or a
            COMMENT: {secure: ...} wrapper is decided at serialize time, below.
    END METHOD

    COMMENT: ====================================================================================
    COMMENT: Where serialization and encryption actually live
    COMMENT: ====================================================================================
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: Execute deliberately has NO prepareForJson()/toObject() override here. Model-
    COMMENT: Generation.md's "Where serialization lives" section is explicit that Execute,
    COMMENT: Request and Response carry only genuine model methods -- no serialization
    COMMENT: overrides -- because the encryption call this class would otherwise need to
    COMMENT: make (core.encryptObject(), for secure components) can be asynchronous on some
    COMMENT: platforms (e.g. WebCrypto), while prepareForJson()/toObject() are specified as
    COMMENT: synchronous. Putting the encryption call here would silently break on any
    COMMENT: platform where it can't be awaited from inside a sync method.
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: Instead, this shape selection belongs in the request helper that builds the
    COMMENT: outgoing payload (the reference libraries call it HttpRequestHelper), as a
    COMMENT: function shaped roughly like this pseudocode -- NOT a method on this class:
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT:   FUNCTION serializeExecute(executeModel: Execute): Object
    COMMENT:       CREATE requestObject WITH {
    COMMENT:           component: executeModel.component,
    COMMENT:           parameters: executeModel.parameters
    COMMENT:       }
    COMMENT:       IF executeModel.componentModel is not null AND
    COMMENT:          executeModel.componentModel.isSecure is true THEN
    COMMENT:           IF executeModel.core is null THEN
    COMMENT:               THROW error "Core is required for encrypting secure components"
    COMMENT:           END IF
    COMMENT:           CREATE encryptedObject AS executeModel.core.encryptObject(requestObject)
    COMMENT:           RETURN { secure: encryptedObject }
    COMMENT:       END IF
    COMMENT:       RETURN requestObject
    COMMENT:   END FUNCTION
